<title>USA: Clinton ready to discuss raising Medicare premium.</title>
<headline>Clinton ready to discuss raising Medicare premium.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton said at a news conference on Tuesday that he would be willing to discuss the possibility of raising premiums paid by wealthy people for the Medicare health care program for the elderly.</p>
<p>&quot;If we're going to have a longer-term Medicare reform I have never said that I would rule that out. But I didn't want to rule it in,&quot; Clinton said. &quot; And I'm prepared to meet with (Republican Senate Majority Leader Trent) Lott and discuss that and other issues.&quot;</p>
</text>
